{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Magnetic circuits",
  "exampleId": "block-magnetic-core",
  "description": "The winding carries 1 A from 1 V through 1 Ω, so it drives 100 A of magnetomotive force round a gap of 10⁶ A/Wb and a core of 10⁵ A/Wb: 90.9 µWb, with 90.9 A of it across the gap. Its inductance N² / R_m = 9.1 mH sets the 9.1 ms rise. Beside it, a constant 100 A drives a reluctance that swings between 1 and 3 · 10⁶ A/Wb, a signal source drives 50 A through a permeance of 1 µWb/A, and a flux source forces 1 mWb through 10⁶ A/Wb, which takes 1000 A.",
  "duration": 0.1,
  "revision": 0,
